    'sections' => [

        ['id' => 'overview', 'eyebrow' => 'Overview', 'h' => 'What happens after MBBS in China', 'p' => [
            "Finishing an MBBS is a real achievement, but it is not the end of the road. A medical degree is a qualification. It is not, by itself, a licence to treat patients. In almost every country, a doctor who wants to practise must also be registered with that country's medical regulator, and a doctor who studied abroad usually has to pass a licensing examination or an assessment first.",
