        ['id' => 'language', 'eyebrow' => 'Language', 'h' => 'Why Chinese and English both matter', 'p' => [
            "Your lectures are in English, but your patients in the clinical years speak Chinese. Introductory Chinese is taught in years 1 and 2, and HSK-4 is required by graduation. Students who take Chinese seriously learn more on the wards, because they can take histories and follow what the doctors are saying.",
